drg: IOSurface CreateChild/WrapClientImage/WrapClientMemory refused (patch 0920)

Boot #58: CoreAnimation's GL path in backboardd called IOSurface selector 6
(WrapClientImage) three times; DrgSurface answered every unknown selector
with success and a zeroed output, so IOSurface.framework built a client
whose state page pointer (lock result +0x08 -> client +0x70) was NULL, and
iosurface_get_edr_factor -> IOSurfaceClientGetBulkAttachments read it:
backboardd SIGSEGV at 0x30, x3. Selectors 1, 6 and 7 (the ones that build a
client from the reply) now return kIOReturnUnsupported; the framework then
returns NULL and CA's retain_image skips the wrap.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/DrgSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/DrgSurface.cpp
index c911c99..672b768 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/DrgSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/DrgSurface.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,10 @@ enum {
 	kDrgSurfaceLimits             = 13,
 	kDrgSurfaceLookupFromPort     = 34,
 	kDrgSurfaceCreatePort         = 35,
+	/* answered with a lock result the framework builds a client from (patch 0920) */
+	kDrgSurfaceCreateChild        = 1,
+	kDrgSurfaceWrapClientImage    = 6,
+	kDrgSurfaceWrapClientMemory   = 7,
 };
 
 enum {
@@ -772,6 +776,20 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::externalMethod(uint32_t selector, IOExternalMethodArgum
 		drg_surf_log_once("sel", selector);
 		return kIOReturnSuccess;
 	}
+	case kDrgSurfaceCreateChild:
+	case kDrgSurfaceWrapClientImage:
+	case kDrgSurfaceWrapClientMemory:
+		/*
+		 * Not supported: refuse, never "succeed" with a zero lock result. IOSurface.framework
+		 * (iOS 16.7: IOSurfaceClientWrapClientImage 0x1a3986580, ...Memory 0x1a3986834,
+		 * ...CreateChild 0x1a398107c) copies the result into a new IOSurfaceClient at +0x68;
+		 * a zero result left its state page (+0x70) NULL, and CoreAnimation's GL path then read
+		 * it in IOSurfaceClientGetBulkAttachments (iosurface_get_edr_factor): backboardd SIGSEGV
+		 * at 0x30, boot #58. On an error the framework returns NULL, and CA's retain_image skips
+		 * the wrap (cbz before wrap_buffer).
+		 */
+		drg_surf_log_once("sel", selector);
+		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
 	default:
 		/* Values, notifications, ownership, timestamps...: accept and ignore. */
 		for (uint32_t i = 0; i < args->scalarOutputCount; i++) {
